# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Node / frontend ---
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Rust / Tauri ---
# `target*` and not `target/`: a scratch build directory beside the real one
# (target-check, used to compile the node's control plane without the engine
# while a release build holds the lock on target/) is not matched by the exact
# name, and 4005 build artefacts went into a commit before this said so.
target*/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# --- Go ---
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# --- Env & secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Not a secret: the console's development API base, needed for a fresh
# checkout to reach the orchestrator at all.
!admin-ui/.env.development
*.pem
*.key
# The signing identity, which is the one secret here whose leak is somebody
# else's problem too: a key that can sign software as us is a key that can sign
# anything as us. `.p12` is the shape it is actually kept in, key and
# certificate together, and it was the one not named.
*.p12
*.cer
*.csr
*.mobileprovision
# The App Store Connect API key, which notarises a release without anybody
# typing a password. Apple shows it once and never again, so a copy in a
# repository is both a leak and the only copy somebody could find.
*.p8

# --- Build / temp artifacts ---
tmp/
*.log
coverage/

# Locally installed dev tools (version-stamped, see Makefile)
.tools/

# A development inference node's own disk: its identity, and any weights it has
# downloaded. Gigabytes, and none of it belongs to anybody but that machine.
inference/data/

# Console
admin-ui/node_modules/
admin-ui/dist/
/orchestrator/sag

# Python bytecode from dev scripts
__pycache__/

# The icon and gate toolchains borrow the chat's node_modules through a link
# rather than installing a second copy of Playwright. The link is made when it
# is missing and must never be committed: it went in once, under the pre-split
# path this used to name, and a Windows checkout turns a symlink into a TEXT
# FILE holding the path, so `node` finds a file where a package should be and
# the icons cannot be drawn at all.
desktop/shared/icons/node_modules
desktop/personal/e2e/node_modules

# Built by `go build ./cmd/...` from inside orchestrator/, which drops the
# binary beside the source rather than in bin/.
orchestrator/sag-payload
# A one-off tool built from orchestrator/internal/nodeca/probe/main.go. The
# source belongs here; a 9 MB binary of it, carrying the absolute paths of
# whoever compiled it, does not. It was committed once.
orchestrator/probe

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The publish gate strips everything between the header above and THIS line.
# It is a marker and not the last entry on purpose: the strip used to end at
# a named rule, so a rule added below it shipped, silently, which is how the
# publish script itself became public. Add internal rules ABOVE this line.

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Keys, certificates and credentials. None of these ever gets committed.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Where they actually live on a build machine. Named as well as pattern-matched,
# because a directory is easier to get right than an extension somebody invents.
apple-signing/
.secrets/
secrets/

# Apple: the Developer ID (signs the app), the App Store Connect key
# (notarises it). Covered by extension above; named here so it is obvious.
*.p12
*.p8
*.cer
*.csr
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile

# Windows code signing: the certificate in every shape it is sold in.
*.pfx
*.spc
*.pvk
*.jks
*.keystore

# The update signing keys, one per edition. A leak of one lets somebody push a
# release to that edition, which is the worst thing on this list.
*.key.pub
sag-updater-*.key*
*.minisign
minisign.pub

# Generic key and certificate shapes.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.der
*.p7b
*.asc
*.gpg
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# What a deployment generates for itself: the encryption key every stored
# credential is sealed with, database passwords, the node join token.
deploy/.env
deploy/*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!admin-ui/.env.development

# Cloud and CI credentials, if any ever land here.
.aws/
.azure/
gcloud-*.json
service-account*.json
